            "paragraph": "To understand these changes, the underlying dynamical background is analyzed. It is found that changes in baroclinicity, static stability, transformation from eddy kinetic energy to kinetic energy of the mean flow and stationary wave activity are significant in particular in the WM and the coastline of North Africa.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": false,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "cyclonic activity",
            "source_entity_type": "Weather_Event",
            "relation": "IMPACTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "southern part of the WM",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "The reduction of cyclonic activity severely impacts the precipitation mainly in the southern part of the WM.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "North African Sharav cyclones",
            "source_entity_type": "Weather_Event",
            "relation": "IMPACTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "North Africa",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "In addition to the above mentioned mid-latitude factors, the MB is affected by episodes of tropical-extra-tropical interactions. These include the Red-Sea trough (Dayan et al. 2001), the North African Sharav cyclones (Alpert and Ziv 1989), and tropical plumes (Ziv 2001; Knippertz 2005).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "North Atlantic Oscillation",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Mediterranean Basin",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Other factors affecting the MB are the North Atlantic Oscillation (Jacobeit et al. 2003) and the West Atlantic-East Russia oscillation (Krichak and Alpert 2005).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "West Atlantic-East Russia oscillation",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Mediterranean Basin",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Other factors affecting the MB are the North Atlantic Oscillation (Jacobeit et al. 2003) and the West Atlantic-East Russia oscillation (Krichak and Alpert 2005).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "El Ni\u00f1o Southern Oscillation",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Mediterranean Basin",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Moreover, there are indications of a possible influence of El Ni\u00f1o Southern Oscillation (ENSO) on the MB (Price et al. 1998; Br\u00f6nnimann 2007), which is, however, still under debate.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
